WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.012 --> 00:00:04.775
(light guitar music)

00:00:05.803 --> 00:00:08.883
- So we want KittyHostel to
be the dog vacay for cats.

00:00:08.883 --> 00:00:10.345
But as you can guess it's a big

00:00:10.345 --> 00:00:12.965
problem that needs big resources.

00:00:12.965 --> 00:00:13.788
- [Man with long hair] Hey.

00:00:13.788 --> 00:00:14.523
- [Blond man] Hey.

00:00:14.523 --> 00:00:15.987
- [Man with long hair]
Excited to have you on board.

00:00:15.987 --> 00:00:17.867
- [Blond man] Oh, on board.

00:00:17.867 --> 00:00:19.733
- You'll be in here today.

00:00:19.733 --> 00:00:22.763
- (sighs) This is nice.

00:00:22.763 --> 00:00:24.720
This is where you do data entry?

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:25.881
(door closes)

00:00:25.881 --> 00:00:28.636
- I know this is weird, but I don't

00:00:28.636 --> 00:00:31.486
actually need you to do anything.

00:00:31.486 --> 00:00:35.038
- Uh, okay, awesome.

00:00:35.038 --> 00:00:39.263
- (sighs) KittyHostel is out of runway.

00:00:39.263 --> 00:00:40.858
- I'm sorry, runway?

00:00:40.858 --> 00:00:42.695
- It's a fancy way of
saying we're out of money.

00:00:42.695 --> 00:00:44.524
There's a group of
investors coming in at noon

00:00:44.524 --> 00:00:46.164
and if they don't put
in, I'm going to have

00:00:46.164 --> 00:00:48.488
to lay off pretty much everyone.

00:00:48.488 --> 00:00:51.090
I need them to think we're
much bigger than we are.

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:54.995
- So, just to be clear here,
you want me to do nothing?

00:00:54.995 --> 00:00:56.417
- Correct.

00:00:56.417 --> 00:00:57.943
- But you are going to pay me.

00:00:57.943 --> 00:01:00.699
- I'll pay you double not to mess this up.

00:01:00.699 --> 00:01:04.382
When I bring the investors
around, just nod and smile.

00:01:04.382 --> 00:01:05.469
No one wants to talk to the

00:01:05.469 --> 00:01:07.687
director of database engineering anyway.

00:01:07.687 --> 00:01:09.706
- Sorry, director of database engineering?

00:01:09.706 --> 00:01:11.090
- That title cool with you?

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:13.683
- Oh, yeah, it's fine, I just-

00:01:13.683 --> 00:01:15.535
- Do you know anyone
else who's available at

00:01:15.535 --> 00:01:18.579
a moment's notice, who
could take this seriously?

00:01:18.579 --> 00:01:21.357
There's a lot on the line.

00:01:21.357 --> 00:01:25.841
- Um, yeah, yeah, I think I do.

00:01:27.998 --> 00:01:29.445
- Well, you can tell the Scottsdale office

00:01:29.445 --> 00:01:31.118
their numbers were shit last quarter.

00:01:31.118 --> 00:01:32.748
- Mm-hmm, yeah, that's
a Taylor Swift song.

00:01:32.748 --> 00:01:33.780
- [Woman] Gimme that.

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:34.840
- Whose dog is this?

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:35.793
- Don't worry about it.

00:01:35.793 --> 00:01:37.525
- You must be Brandon's sister.

00:01:37.525 --> 00:01:38.957
- Not today.

00:01:38.957 --> 00:01:41.013
Sorry, that's the last
time I break character.

00:01:41.013 --> 00:01:42.908
You must be our fearless visionary.

00:01:42.908 --> 00:01:44.249
- Oh, sorry, she-

00:01:44.249 --> 00:01:45.554
- N-n-n-no.

00:01:45.554 --> 00:01:47.845
I like it.

00:01:47.845 --> 00:01:49.007
This'll work.

00:01:49.007 --> 00:01:50.061
- Uh, what?

00:01:50.061 --> 00:01:51.354
- You say the right things.

00:01:51.354 --> 00:01:53.173
- I will live, breathe,
and sleep this company.

00:01:53.173 --> 00:01:55.162
I'll stop at nothing until we're

00:01:55.162 --> 00:01:58.169
leaders in whatever our market is.

00:01:58.169 --> 00:01:59.406
- I get it, you're a killer.

00:01:59.406 --> 00:02:00.584
- I'm your killer.

00:02:00.584 --> 00:02:01.600
Now what's my title?

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:04.719
- You seem like a VP of
customer acquisitions.

00:02:04.719 --> 00:02:05.694
- Love it.

00:02:05.694 --> 00:02:08.033
I'll acquire the shit out
of fake customers for you.

00:02:08.033 --> 00:02:09.536
- That's the fire we need.

00:02:09.536 --> 00:02:10.863
You'll take Brandon's office.

00:02:10.863 --> 00:02:12.232
- Uh, excuse me, but-

00:02:12.232 --> 00:02:13.880
- It just makes sense.

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:15.204
The investors will be here in an hour.

00:02:15.204 --> 00:02:17.763
Brandon, make sure she knows the drill.

00:02:17.763 --> 00:02:19.624
- Oh, shoot, I'm going
to have to call David and

00:02:19.624 --> 00:02:21.106
tell him I won't be
home in time for dinner.

00:02:21.106 --> 00:02:22.118
- Who's David?

00:02:22.118 --> 00:02:22.967
- My husband.

00:02:22.967 --> 00:02:24.203
We met at Stanford Business School.

00:02:24.203 --> 00:02:26.461
- Okay, this guy is going to pay us

00:02:26.461 --> 00:02:30.103
double to sit in a room
and not cause any trouble.

00:02:30.103 --> 00:02:33.337
Not to treat this like an
audition for the Social Network 2.

00:02:33.337 --> 00:02:34.858
- No Brandon, you don't get it.

00:02:34.858 --> 00:02:36.382
This is a happening, okay?

00:02:36.382 --> 00:02:39.017
I nail this, I'm the lead
in a workplace sitcom.

00:02:39.017 --> 00:02:40.803
- Look, I've gone through a lot of these

00:02:40.803 --> 00:02:43.182
temp gigs already, and
this is the first one

00:02:43.182 --> 00:02:45.322
that has any long-term potential.

00:02:45.322 --> 00:02:47.569
I mean, this guy's
paying me to do nothing.

00:02:47.569 --> 00:02:49.355
I could do this forever.

00:02:49.355 --> 00:02:50.843
We could do this forever.

00:02:50.843 --> 00:02:52.181
- I don't know.

00:02:52.181 --> 00:02:53.922
Right now we need to focus on inhabiting

00:02:53.922 --> 00:02:55.664
our environment, so we can become

00:02:55.664 --> 00:02:57.447
one with the workplace milieu.

00:02:57.447 --> 00:02:58.992
- No, n-n-n-no, no inhabitation.

00:02:58.992 --> 00:03:01.143
That's going to be your office there.

00:03:01.143 --> 00:03:03.347
I'm going to find a cubicle.

00:03:03.347 --> 00:03:05.635
Try to reign this in.

00:03:05.635 --> 00:03:07.417
- Don't talk to your superior that way.

00:03:07.417 --> 00:03:09.048
Scottsdale, back on the line.

00:03:09.048 --> 00:03:10.934
How are you, motherfuckers?

00:03:10.934 --> 00:03:14.307
(light guitar music)

00:03:14.307 --> 00:03:16.728
(phone rings)

00:03:16.728 --> 00:03:17.583
- Hi?

00:03:17.583 --> 00:03:19.350
- Hey, figured you'd want to see

00:03:19.350 --> 00:03:21.439
the latest server load reports.

00:03:21.439 --> 00:03:23.022
- I, I don't.

00:03:23.022 --> 00:03:25.643
- But the database is
running out of memory.

00:03:25.643 --> 00:03:28.417
- Did, did Brittney put you up to this?

00:03:28.417 --> 00:03:29.753
- The new VP?

00:03:29.753 --> 00:03:30.864
- You're real?

00:03:30.864 --> 00:03:32.923
Sorry, you're a real employee, here?

00:03:32.923 --> 00:03:34.771
- I'm part-time, but...

00:03:34.771 --> 00:03:36.993
- Oh, ah, never mind.

00:03:36.993 --> 00:03:39.552
So the database is running out of memory?

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:40.806
That sounds bad.

00:03:40.806 --> 00:03:41.880
- Seems like cacheing our most

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:44.005
recent queries would reduce the strain.

00:03:44.005 --> 00:03:46.242
- Do we have to buy
anything for that to happen?

00:03:46.242 --> 00:03:48.308
- No, just takes a couple lines of code.

00:03:48.308 --> 00:03:49.798
But, do you think there'll be any

00:03:49.798 --> 00:03:52.250
issues with backwards compatibility?

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:57.215
- Compatibility sounds positive.

00:03:57.215 --> 00:03:59.496
Yeah, I think you should go for it.

00:03:59.496 --> 00:04:01.510
- Okay, I'm on it.

00:04:04.134 --> 00:04:06.661
- Good job.

00:04:06.661 --> 00:04:08.169
- Thanks.

00:04:11.597 --> 00:04:13.491
(phone rings)

00:04:13.491 --> 00:04:14.813
- Hello?

00:04:14.813 --> 00:04:16.226
- [Voice on phone] I have
Brittany calling for Brandon.

00:04:16.226 --> 00:04:17.396
- Brittney.

00:04:17.396 --> 00:04:18.638
- Please hold for Brittney.

00:04:18.638 --> 00:04:20.155
The investors are here.

00:04:20.155 --> 00:04:21.686
Showtime.

00:04:21.686 --> 00:04:23.241
- No, there's no showtime.

00:04:23.241 --> 00:04:24.551
Brittney.

00:04:24.551 --> 00:04:25.570
- [Man in grey shirt] That's Brandon.

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:27.868
He's our database engineer.

00:04:27.868 --> 00:04:29.401
Once we reach critical mass in

00:04:29.401 --> 00:04:32.687
Los Angeles, San Francisco is next.

00:04:32.687 --> 00:04:35.005
- Have you found a scalable
acquisition strategy?

00:04:35.005 --> 00:04:35.715
- Well-

00:04:35.715 --> 00:04:38.468
- Well that depends on
your definition of scale.

00:04:38.468 --> 00:04:40.858
How about we go into my office
for a brief presentation.

00:04:40.858 --> 00:04:42.378
- Uh, not now, Brittney.

00:04:42.378 --> 00:04:44.459
Maybe after we go over the financials.

00:04:44.459 --> 00:04:45.233
- Sounds good.

00:04:45.233 --> 00:04:46.121
I'll sit in.

00:04:46.121 --> 00:04:47.544
Follow me.

00:04:47.544 --> 00:04:48.774
How are you guys doing?

00:04:48.774 --> 00:04:49.820
You look thinner.

00:04:49.820 --> 00:04:52.173
- Uh, actually, sorry guys, I have

00:04:52.173 --> 00:04:56.798
a meeting with Brittney now to
discuss scaling the database.

00:04:56.798 --> 00:04:59.508
- Scale, yes, talk to me about scale.

00:04:59.508 --> 00:05:02.023
Chase tells me he's got a saddle on

00:05:02.023 --> 00:05:06.007
a unicorn that's ready to shit gold.

00:05:06.007 --> 00:05:09.382
- Okay, well our first step is

00:05:09.382 --> 00:05:13.430
to cache all recent queries.

00:05:13.430 --> 00:05:15.382
This doesn't cost anything up front,

00:05:15.382 --> 00:05:18.987
but it should reduce a lot
of strain in the long run.

00:05:18.987 --> 00:05:20.221
- Makes sense.

00:05:20.221 --> 00:05:22.436
- See, I built a world-class team.

00:05:22.436 --> 00:05:24.145
(knocking on door)

00:05:24.145 --> 00:05:25.453
- Sir, the database change you

00:05:25.453 --> 00:05:27.405
authorized caused a kernel panic.

00:05:27.405 --> 00:05:30.476
- You authorized a database change?

00:05:30.476 --> 00:05:33.261
- Uh, yeah, a couple of lines of code.

00:05:33.261 --> 00:05:35.635
- Well you do know how to fix it, right?

00:05:35.635 --> 00:05:39.065
- Yeah, you made him the
director of database engineering.

00:05:39.065 --> 00:05:40.554
- You guys need a moment?

00:05:40.554 --> 00:05:44.316
- No, this will just take a second.

00:05:44.316 --> 00:05:45.617
- [Brandon] Look I think what-

00:05:45.617 --> 00:05:46.920
- [Chase] I'm not paying you to think.

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:49.287
I'm paying you not to fuck up.

00:05:49.287 --> 00:05:51.337
And you did, royally.

00:05:51.337 --> 00:05:52.424
- Hey.

00:05:52.424 --> 00:05:53.573
- He's right.

00:05:53.573 --> 00:05:56.622
- Look, I don't need any input
from a lunatic bitch, either.

00:05:56.622 --> 00:05:59.558
- Hey.

00:05:59.558 --> 00:06:01.020
Now, you're not going to let him talk

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:02.679
to an executive of your stature

00:06:02.679 --> 00:06:04.360
that way now, are you, Brittney?

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:05.762
- Certainly not.

00:06:05.762 --> 00:06:07.806
You just remember who pays
the bills around here.

00:06:07.806 --> 00:06:08.681
- What?

00:06:08.681 --> 00:06:10.161
- Yeah, Daddy didn't cut you a check

00:06:10.161 --> 00:06:12.852
and put us on the board for
you to just shit all over us.

00:06:12.852 --> 00:06:16.509
- Whoa, trouble at the unicorn farm.

00:06:16.509 --> 00:06:18.513
- What the hell are you talking about?

00:06:18.513 --> 00:06:19.612
I'm really sorry.

00:06:19.612 --> 00:06:20.900
- No, I'm really sorry.

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:22.960
I expected more from
our portfolio companies.

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:23.878
- You invested?

00:06:23.878 --> 00:06:24.760
- Daddy did.

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:26.051
- Yeah, that's right.

00:06:26.051 --> 00:06:29.501
It's, uh, Daddy's money that's
in those unicorn saddle bags.

00:06:29.501 --> 00:06:31.379
- Yeah, and we have
first-in first-out shares,

00:06:31.379 --> 00:06:33.397
which I'm sure Chase told you all about.

00:06:33.397 --> 00:06:34.731
- He did not.

00:06:34.731 --> 00:06:38.070
Look, I think we all have
a lot to think about.

00:06:38.070 --> 00:06:40.183
So, we'll be in touch.

00:06:40.183 --> 00:06:41.759
Do you have a card?

00:06:41.759 --> 00:06:43.765
I'd love to get together to talk shop.

00:06:43.765 --> 00:06:45.289
- Voila.

00:06:45.289 --> 00:06:46.998
I do magic.

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:53.508
(door closes)

00:06:53.508 --> 00:06:54.681
- You're fired.

00:06:54.681 --> 00:06:55.669
- No shit.

00:06:55.669 --> 00:06:58.392
- Yeah, you can't treat
people like wet garbage.

00:06:58.392 --> 00:07:00.615
Call the car.

00:07:00.615 --> 00:07:03.655
- Uh, yes, would you bring
the car around, please.

00:07:03.655 --> 00:07:05.105
- Nice.

00:07:05.105 --> 00:07:06.882
- You know, that was kind of awesome.

00:07:06.882 --> 00:07:07.939
- I know.

00:07:07.939 --> 00:07:10.431
Scottsdale, your sales team sack-up yet?

00:07:10.431 --> 00:07:12.410
- Hey, what happened to that dog?

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:13.422
- [Brittney] Don't worry about it.

00:07:13.422 --> 00:07:14.773
I stole it.

00:07:14.773 --> 00:07:19.773
(light guitar music)

00:07:22.081 --> 00:07:25.351
(dog growling)

00:07:28.069 --> 00:07:29.883
(projector clicking)

00:07:29.883 --> 00:07:34.883
(synthesized strings tone)

